 "selection": "Two checks, decided before applying. (1) Along the measured shoulder motions of Seth et al. 2019 (Front Neurorobot 13:90, doi:10.3389/fnbot.2019.00090; 18 abduction/flexion/shrug trials, IK), for muscles whose myoarm fibre length correlates r >= 0.8 with the Seth model's (deltoids, latissimus, pectoralis, teres major, coracobrachialis, biceps long head): adopted when the MoBL-direct map's normalised fibre length is closer to Seth's (RMSE) with no more frames outside 0.5-1.5. (2) Muscles whose myoarm path agrees with MoBL-ARMS within 5 % l0 over 400 full-range postures: adopted when fibre length moves closer to OpenSim's and isometric force error rises by at most 2 % Fmax. Rotator cuff, TRIlong and the forearm/hand extrinsics are not converted (scapular kinematics differ from Seth's; hand extrinsics are refit against passive moments in Vittorio-Caggiano/myo_sim#2).",
